{"title":"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-sided polygon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0fef2a783971fc08bd075a80546c6242e0ed9f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGHIJKL$\" width=\"168\" height=\"13\" />, as shown. Each of its sides has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and each two consecutive sides form a right angle. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f0f6aa257bd96696d97454bb777b1a283069e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AG}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf06e5af8cfb43ec7280a9e284f6a338d8b6175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CH}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d4180c1fb3d692aaacf48a8f066c4f6fc1acb7bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCM$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1398362ab7277efd803b7326d6c586d92b193210.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(13mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(1,3), B=(2,3), C=(2,2), D=(3,2), Ep=(3,1), F=(2,1), G=(2,0), H=(1,0), I=(1,1), J=(0,1), K=(0,2), L=(1,2); pair M=intersectionpoints(A--G,H--C)[0];  draw(A--B--C--D--Ep--F--G--H--I--J--K--L--cycle); draw(A--G); draw(H--C); dot(M);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,Ep,SE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,SE); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,SW); label(&quot;$I$&quot;,I,SW); label(&quot;$J$&quot;,J,SW); label(&quot;$K$&quot;,K,NW); label(&quot;$L$&quot;,L,NW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,W); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a703ff8c8741ef37104a44da8142fe7070b322b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac {44}{3}\\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 16 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\frac {88}{5}\\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\frac {62}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"390\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can obtain the solution by calculating the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c109a8ffe32014813d961109ba8b2ded63772d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABGH$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> minus the combined area of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99dc01734e30b381a1aa488537a0388dbca88def.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AHG$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a013638eb175a47c098e47bd0a81080afda7da81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CGM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We know that triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57d081d595dc6773062577ae05f4ca20019b2d02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AMH$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b6376ec20d31a8c7cc946d91ca27e4e5b5c9b2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GMC$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> are similar because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b0b4a41229f41b7edd4adcbd3def0f8a008ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AH} \\parallel \\overline{CG}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />. Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c85382bd4ccb9b2c36d4ff7c6324e9834307f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AH}{CG} = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />, the ratio of the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5605e7674254425ca5932c0a752f8a04b6b16770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AH}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> to the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8ddc7b8c702ae12dacad9c833f53fc173066c622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CG}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfdbd19877c13d1755e01b54ba640f512c883a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Solving with the fact that the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5605e7674254425ca5932c0a752f8a04b6b16770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AH}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8ddc7b8c702ae12dacad9c833f53fc173066c622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CG}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is 4, we see that the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8ddc7b8c702ae12dacad9c833f53fc173066c622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CG}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/778abab8ebf560b512a9a7e95a1c404065dc9cb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99dc01734e30b381a1aa488537a0388dbca88def.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AHG$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b796eac2b0a571d7debceed0f344dde8c775a6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4 \\cdot 12 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"109\" height=\"37\" />, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a013638eb175a47c098e47bd0a81080afda7da81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CGM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/6785373ed3261e0c907bd7fb414b9a4120883280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{8}{5} \\cdot 8 = \\frac{32}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"37\" />, and the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c109a8ffe32014813d961109ba8b2ded63772d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABGH$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d589e6009c41c09f064dadebe7ea6d2a53743c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 12 = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Taking the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c109a8ffe32014813d961109ba8b2ded63772d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABGH$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and subtracting the combined area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99dc01734e30b381a1aa488537a0388dbca88def.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AHG$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a013638eb175a47c098e47bd0a81080afda7da81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CGM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955277e20a287a66660cc04762da4199d0c0032c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48 - \\left(24 + \\frac{32}{5}\\right) = \\boxed{\\frac{88}{5}}\\ \\text{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"219\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/64721f756f1c801d9696fe36e45507773be011b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(1,3), B=(2,3), C=(2,2), D=(3,2), Ep=(3,1), F=(2,1), G=(2,0), H=(1,0), I=(1,1), J=(0,1), K=(0,2), L=(1,2); pair M=intersectionpoints(A--G,H--C)[0]; pair Z=(2.5,3);  draw(A--B--C--D--Ep--F--G--H--I--J--K--L--cycle); draw(A--G); draw(H--C); draw(B--Z--C); draw(C--F); dot(M);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,Ep,SE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,SE); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,SW); label(&quot;$I$&quot;,I,SW); label(&quot;$J$&quot;,J,SW); label(&quot;$K$&quot;,K,NW); label(&quot;$L$&quot;,L,NW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,W); label(&quot;$N$&quot;,Z,NE); [/asy]\" width=\"325\" height=\"322\" />\n</p><p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8e26d580012b86d8fe55e70e5740908c35af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> and call their intersection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/576d595084e2a94ac3eb1c2ee067562030dd825d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CBN$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10d021bbf3c6a09ec084e2f20b3752a85aa4937.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CGH$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> are clearly similar with ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e1a1a7adf986532b7598e896785a56c785f779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76dbb36ee3e49fc6ad1e92e43bb98560193a7795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BN=2$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a28afe2cd30888e82cba0c28deb2d6df5e995e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN=6$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />. The area of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036bf5e5bf3938a62201c696cf6051b5509be494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCN$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50be8838823e86b768d2fd3aefa6093a51270e21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\cdot 4}2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcbd24f888801c82be1dd75b1cc4b0d7a160f0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MAN$\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f0a8fc3106b64b4666cfeb5c178dfbe4d35746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MGH$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> are similar as well, and we now know that the ratio of their dimensions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d42d298f1005b627b53683d668a878a9b2c0499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN:GH = 6:4 = 3:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"191\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Draw altitudes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7a248cfd02095e2a009f811d5732a9bea9d595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />, let their feet be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6a4a0680d4e0668219585d856c7f109cd09f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c879631d01bcc51ec112e4a32a039f624d40c91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />. We get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378fcec1210f5749828cd5a0e8dac1f93dc9d400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MM_1 : MM_2 = 3:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"15\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1aa20b2a7c167ab60d9fcd383d395a661238794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MM_1 = \\frac 35 \\cdot 12 = \\frac {36}5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" />. (An alternate way is by seeing that the set-up AHGCM is similar to the 2 pole problem (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\">http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30</a>). Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460fdf918ae5a80d5aae3784ad89817d960499ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MM_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4d8a87f47b20ac6b62efb935b3c0048a7fd143a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{12}} = \\frac{24}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"99\" height=\"43\" />, by the harmonic mean. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/15458d6b968290feda8dfc4a1f8426dec75028f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MM_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01dd532bb72d26ccb1ac3325d7c6569e40977ca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.)   \n</p><p>Then the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90aa302feed3983e7156a34b821ad877642919b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMN$\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a90acda8c5e1953665558891984833e4aaeccf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12 \\cdot AN \\cdot MM_1 = \\frac{108}5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"168\" height=\"37\" />, and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d4180c1fb3d692aaacf48a8f066c4f6fc1acb7bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCM$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> can be obtained by subtracting the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036bf5e5bf3938a62201c696cf6051b5509be494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCN$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b65e811774898d8347be11cd55a4ef6d6232bd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{108}5 - 4 =  \\boxed{\\frac{88}5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"120\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1398362ab7277efd803b7326d6c586d92b193210.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(13mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(1,3), B=(2,3), C=(2,2), D=(3,2), Ep=(3,1), F=(2,1), G=(2,0), H=(1,0), I=(1,1), J=(0,1), K=(0,2), L=(1,2); pair M=intersectionpoints(A--G,H--C)[0];  draw(A--B--C--D--Ep--F--G--H--I--J--K--L--cycle); draw(A--G); draw(H--C); dot(M);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,Ep,SE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,SE); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,SW); label(&quot;$I$&quot;,I,SW); label(&quot;$J$&quot;,J,SW); label(&quot;$K$&quot;,K,NW); label(&quot;$L$&quot;,L,NW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,W); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p>We can use coordinates to solve this. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d32e656f121ea92ac7c093fbb988905fca6bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H=(0,0).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5121dc3b75fb4a457cfceb23c5c3c79d02fdcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(0,12), C=(4,8), G=(4,0).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"265\" height=\"18\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> has equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a0f3fac311230251de91efd99b500d3451b6718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3x+12=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb82bca7de59684e050803ba493e050e355614f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HC$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> has equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd873d4c595edc4ec5b30468f234d3e04cbc1903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x=y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" /> Solving, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/addef7b8d40ef7f6d3b49caccb09a579f6d67c72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=(\\frac {12}{5},\\frac {24}{5}).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" /> Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shoelace_Theorem\" title=\"Shoelace Theorem\">Shoelace Theorem</a> (or you could connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/290b753dd098f48a53d57bf3b755c9756e11c7e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LC$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and solve for the resulting triangle + trapezoid areas), we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d8b0e62f4e452e57d1fb1ad55c9d4c49a0696da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABCM]=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ }\\dfrac{88}{5}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"166\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~(minor edits by Arcticturn)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff13de4340101ffda410fbf96485fed9d9f2725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J = (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> so we can find the equations of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb82bca7de59684e050803ba493e050e355614f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HC$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />, and find the coordinates of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We find the equation of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbf6f98bdf5f515e51249928ed7c3228530ad800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -3x + 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" /> and line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb82bca7de59684e050803ba493e050e355614f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HC$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/3342ddb7152233ec64f5b07c0eb8eb4e3e967db7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2x + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />. Setting these equations equal to each other, we solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d4eac00382943ae74d6f02e0b6965ab701acdbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-3x + 20 = 2x + 12 \\implies x = \\frac{8}{5}\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"37\" />\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> back in gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad5521f921eb81f578c8b336f22f485c7d869b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\left(\\frac{32}{5}, \\frac{4}{5}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"115\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>We can also find the area of the smaller triangle in the top square by substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a79da7e7844d252be666cb25e2ed8a2c9a96e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> into our equations to see that the base segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/290b753dd098f48a53d57bf3b755c9756e11c7e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LC$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is split into two segments of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24f4606bd5646f403a4676964fe7fea017583c28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, respectively. \n</p><p>The area of this smaller triangle portion is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/623448880f8f3c4593ca77841ab110fc97fe683c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4 \\times \\frac{4}{3}}{2} = \\frac{8}{3}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting this from the total area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we find that the top portion of the quadrilateral's area is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a4442a790fe17e39eb126cfa6512affff4c0e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16 - \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{40}{3}\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>For the bottom triangle portion with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24f4606bd5646f403a4676964fe7fea017583c28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, the height is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f02450a161da2805f4beb6dd527529b184271864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 - \\frac{4}{5} = \\frac{16}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />. The area of this triangle is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1a9dcffb85e642191a3f32d62519bb8dca58bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{8}{3} \\times \\frac{16}{5}}{2} = \\frac{64}{15}\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Finally, adding the two areas together gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8c45849eef92d4c28e5d5a84eb572ec8ba629c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{40}{3} + \\frac{64}{15} = \\frac{200}{15} + \\frac{64}{15} = \\frac{264}{15} = \\frac{88}{5}\\]\" width=\"264\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f452e3723b77277876c99185b82f05465c03e1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{88}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"66\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A\">2007 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195100\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 613/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19763/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.131      1 -total\n 61.73%    8.723      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 37.19%    5.255      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6345:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195100 and revision id 288062. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}